KNOWNBUG (unsound): [expr.prim.lambda.closure] -- a mutable lambda's by-copy
captures are mutable non-static data members of the closure object, so
modifications persist across calls of the same closure.  CBMC has no per-object
closure state, so the mutable counter does not persist.  See
doc/architectural/cpp-lambda-closure-support.md.
